@startuml
title Velocity edit: shaping a ramp, then playing it

actor User
participant "TimelineView.Velocity" as TV
participant TimelineEditor
participant SetSpeedCurveCommand as Cmd
participant ClipTime
participant "Preview / export" as Pic
participant AudioMixer

== add a curve ==
User -> TV : clip menu, Add speed curve
TV -> TimelineEditor : AddSpeedCurve(clip)
TimelineEditor -> Cmd : keys [0: Speed, DurSec: Speed]
note right : flat line at the clip's speed:\nnothing changes until a point moves

== shape it ==
User -> TV : double-click the line on a beat
TV -> TimelineEditor : SetSpeedCurve(keys + new point)
User -> TV : drag the point down (slower)
loop while dragging
  TV -> TimelineEditor : SetSpeedCurve(keys, gesture)
  TimelineEditor -> Cmd : coalesced into one undo step
  Cmd -> ClipTime : SrcOut = SourceAt(DurSec)
end
note right of TV : the clip keeps its place and length;\nit just uses less footage

== play ==
Pic -> ClipTime : SourceAt(clip, t)
ClipTime --> Pic : SrcIn + area under the curve up to t
AudioMixer -> ClipTime : SourceAt for every output sample
note right : pitch follows the speed

== cut through a ramp ==
User -> TimelineEditor : split at t
TimelineEditor -> ClipTime : SplitKeyframes(left, right, t)\nright.SrcIn = SourceAt(t)
note right : both halves play exactly as the whole did
@enduml
